{"title":"Open interval","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>An <b>open interval</b> is an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Interval\" title=\"Interval\">interval</a> which has neither a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Maximum\" title=\"Maximum\">maximum</a> nor a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Minimum\" title=\"Minimum\">minimum</a> element. Open intervals are denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Greatest_lower_bound\" title=\"Greatest lower bound\"> infimum</a> (greatest lower bound) and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Least_upper_bound\" title=\"Least upper bound\"> supremum</a> (least upper bound). Alternatively, an open interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Set\" title=\"Set\">set</a> of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> satisfies both of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Inequality\" title=\"Inequality\">inequalities</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/e/dee577de87a897fba96ff88108acd587b2409030.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f87bae4e1be45e1aa97a25f6ffca964dd954e3c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>In an open interval, it is possible that either the infimum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> or the supremum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, or both, do not exist. If the infimum is nonexistent, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afac538740054d4786c170ef0123850adea5cdf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" />; if the supremum is nonexistent, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/7/b671f1bb7e4ee86584347d5d22f1dc8abdb5bef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"9\" />. The corresponding inequality is always considered true in these cases, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/8/938a100772fb3f1540eef936a0f2dfe6a74f89ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\infty &lt; x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/2/822b8a306581e08cd78d63407ebf9b9bbcce2255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; +\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" /> by definition.\n</p><p>Every open interval is an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Open_set\" title=\"Open set\">open set</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Examples\">Examples</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Open_interval&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Examples\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/7/987ff67647968fa49f420b2947548a9f609505ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb R$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />, the set of all <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_numbers\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Real numbers\">real numbers</a>, is an open interval with neither an upper bound nor a lower bound.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/f/7ffbe30784d3580dab3ae39decffd0b5c70e6cf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, + \\infty)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" />, the set of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Positive\">positive</a> real numbers, is an open interval with a lower bound but no upper bound.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/b/9ebecc026757cb2d4f94963508998599bff6aa09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-\\infty, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" />, the set of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Negative\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Negative\">negative</a> real numbers, is an open interval with an upper bound but no lower bound.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/9/149f6a15ba033bfb273e7af037a90ffe9dbaa218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />, the set of real numbers <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Strict_inequality\" title=\"Strict inequality\">strictly</a> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, is an open interval with both an upper bound and a lower bound.\n</p><p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Empty_set\" title=\"Empty set\">empty set</a>, having no elements and therefore neither a maximum nor a minimum, is considered an open interval.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Open_interval&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Closed_interval\" title=\"Closed interval\">Closed interval</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Open_interval&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018102157\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.039 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 135/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 280/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3828/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n10